  "bug": {
    "bug_id": "JacksonDatabind-84",
    "project": "JacksonDatabind",
    "summary": "No title",
    "description": "When a type hierarchy as follows is constructed and the base class' type is constructed first by the TypeFactory then serializing the sub class fails due to missing properties from the base class.\n\nclass Base implements IFace<Sub> { @JsonProperty int base = 1 }\nclass Sub { @JsonProperty int sub = 2 }\ninterface IFace<T> {}\n\nSerializes sub as \n{\"sub\":2}\nwhere \n{\"base\":1,\"sub\":2}\nis expected.\n\nI've created a minimal scenario of this bug here: \nhttps://github.com/slobo-showbie/jackson-recursive-type-bug\n\nI've experienced this bug in 2.7.8, 2.8.8, and 2.8.8.1"
  },
